        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "f43f29f3-6fca-50ad-8707-88e7009102e3",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: The Jungle Book 2, The Jungle Book, The Second Jungle Book, Many Inventions, In the Rukh\n- Companies: DisneyToon Studios, Walt Disney Pictures, Buena Vista Distribution\n- People: Rudyard Kipling, Haley Joel Osment, John Goodman\n- Characters: Mowgli, Baloo\n- Places: Pench area, Seoni, India\n- Concepts: fictional characters, feral children, sequels\n\nFacts:\n- In 1893, Rudyard Kipling introduced Mowgli in the short story \"In the Rukh,\" which was collected in \"Many Inventions.\"\n- In 1894 and 1895, Rudyard Kipling featured Mowgli prominently in \"The Jungle Book\" and \"The Second Jungle Book.\"\n- Mowgli is a fictional character, the protagonist of Rudyard Kipling's \"The Jungle Book\" stories, and a naked feral child from the Pench area in Seoni, India.\n- Walt Disney's film \"The Jungle Book\" was released in 1967.\n- \"The Jungle Book 2\" is a 2003 animated film produced by DisneyToon Studios and released by Walt Disney Pictures and Buena Vista Distribution.\n- \"The Jungle Book 2\" is a sequel to Walt Disney's 1967 film \"The Jungle Book.\"\n- In \"The Jungle Book 2,\" Haley Joel Osment voices Mowgli and John Goodman voices Baloo.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "4b47f9c5-358f-52d0-9cf9-ab6667cd35dd",
        "text": "Page: The Jungle Book 2. Sentence: The Jungle Book 2 is a 2003 animated film produced by DisneyToon Studios and released by Walt Disney Pictures and Buena Vista Distribution.\nPage: The Jungle Book 2. Sentence: The film is a sequel to Walt Disney's 1967 film \"The Jungle Book\", and stars Haley Joel Osment as the voice of Mowgli and John Goodman as the voice of Baloo.\nPage: Mowgli. Sentence: Mowgli is a fictional character and the protagonist of Rudyard Kipling's \"The Jungle Book\" stories.\nPage: Mowgli. Sentence: He is a naked feral child from the Pench area in Seoni, India, who originally appeared in Kipling's short story \"In the Rukh\" (collected in \"Many Inventions\", 1893) and then went on to become the most prominent and memorable character in his collections \"The Jungle Book\" and \"The Second Jungle Book\" (1894–1895), which also featured stories about other characters.",
